    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.notify\n\n### Description\n\nI think putting snippet pasted below in the help file could improve the experience of new users. Especially because it is not a matter of setting one variable in config, but a more involved process.\r\n\r\nLifted straight from https://old.reddit.com/r/neovim/comments/18ye17d/mininotify_show_notifications_a_vimnotify_maker/kgeqnvn/\r\n```lua\r\nlocal win_config = function()\r\n  local has_statusline = vim.o.laststatus > 0\r\n  local bottom_space = vim.o.cmdheight + (has_statusline and 1 or 0)\r\n  return { anchor = \"SE\", col = vim.o.columns, row = vim.o.lines - bottom_space }\r\nend\r\nrequire(\"mini.notify\").setup({ window = { config = win_config } })\r\n```",
